@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il30-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-64a2-fund-definitions`

-- Tests for s 64A2 (definitions for the real-estate investment fund). Expected values were worked by hand from the definitions before they were run.
-- All figures are HYPOTHETICAL.

§ `Tests of section 64A2`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN income IS A BOOLEAN
      built  IS A NUMBER
      allowed IS A NUMBER
      minister IS A BOOLEAN
      inventory IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A parcel of land held by a real-estate investment fund`
`a parcel:` income `, built` built `, buildable` allowed `, ministerial use managed by the fund` minister `, inventory` inventory MEANS
    `A parcel of land held by a real-estate investment fund` WITH
        `income under section 2(1) or 2(6) arises from letting it and from activity ancillary to the letting, apart from a passing break` IS income
        `the total area of the buildings on it` IS built
        `the area that may be built under the plan that applies to it` IS allowed
        `it is for a use the Minister of Finance fixed, and the fund or a relative of it provides the management services` IS minister
        `it is the fund's business inventory` IS inventory

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      k IS A `The kind of income of a real-estate investment fund`
GIVETH AN `An item of income of a real-estate investment fund`
`an item of` a `of the kind` k MEANS
    `An item of income of a real-estate investment fund` WITH
        `the kind` IS k
        `the amount` IS a

`the inventory kind` MEANS `income from the sale of business inventory`
`the yielding kind` MEANS `income from yielding land, land under construction, land for rental housing, or from the sale of building rights in land that was yielding when bought`
`the securities kind` MEANS `income from securities traded on the stock exchange, from state bonds or from deposits`
`the early rental-housing sale kind` MEANS `income from the sale of land for rental housing sold before 20 years of letting it as housing, other than a sale to a landlord`
`the early construction sale kind` MEANS `income from the sale of land that was under construction when bought, sold within four years of its first being used for letting`

§§ `Yielding land`
-- 700 square metres built of 1,000 that may be built: 70%, "at least 70%": yes. 699: no.
#ASSERT `s 64A2 — the land is yielding land` (`a parcel:` TRUE `, built` 700 `, buildable` 1000 `, ministerial use managed by the fund` FALSE `, inventory` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 64A2 — the land is yielding land` (`a parcel:` TRUE `, built` 699 `, buildable` 1000 `, ministerial use managed by the fund` FALSE `, inventory` FALSE)
-- No letting income: no.  A ministerial use managed by the fund or a relative: no.  Business inventory: no.
#ASSERT NOT `s 64A2 — the land is yielding land` (`a parcel:` FALSE `, built` 900 `, buildable` 1000 `, ministerial use managed by the fund` FALSE `, inventory` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 64A2 — the land is yielding land` (`a parcel:` TRUE `, built` 900 `, buildable` 1000 `, ministerial use managed by the fund` TRUE `, inventory` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 64A2 — the land is yielding land` (`a parcel:` TRUE `, built` 900 `, buildable` 1000 `, ministerial use managed by the fund` FALSE `, inventory` TRUE)
-- A land that is wholly built: yes.
#ASSERT `s 64A2 — the land is yielding land` (`a parcel:` TRUE `, built` 1000 `, buildable` 1000 `, ministerial use managed by the fund` FALSE `, inventory` FALSE)

§§ `Exceptional income (fork R1)`
-- Inventory 100 ; yielding 700 ; early rental-housing sale 40 ; early construction sale 25 ; securities 75 ; other 60. The whole: 1,000. 5% of it: 50.
--   The fixed part: 100 + 40 + 25 = 165.  The other income 60 is above 50: the whole 60 is exceptional (225) or the part above 50, 10 (175).
#ASSERT `s 64A2 — the exceptional income of the fund among` (LIST `an item of` 100 `of the kind` `the inventory kind`, `an item of` 700 `of the kind` `the yielding kind`, `an item of` 40 `of the kind` `the early rental-housing sale kind`, `an item of` 25 `of the kind` `the early construction sale kind`, `an item of` 75 `of the kind` `the securities kind`, `an item of` 60 `of the kind` `other income`) `, reading the 5% test as` `all the other income is exceptional once it is more than 5%` EQUALS 225
#ASSERT `s 64A2 — the exceptional income of the fund among` (LIST `an item of` 100 `of the kind` `the inventory kind`, `an item of` 700 `of the kind` `the yielding kind`, `an item of` 40 `of the kind` `the early rental-housing sale kind`, `an item of` 25 `of the kind` `the early construction sale kind`, `an item of` 75 `of the kind` `the securities kind`, `an item of` 60 `of the kind` `other income`) `, reading the 5% test as` `only the part of the other income above 5% is exceptional` EQUALS 175
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 64A2 — the exceptional income of the fund among` (LIST `an item of` 100 `of the kind` `the inventory kind`, `an item of` 700 `of the kind` `the yielding kind`, `an item of` 40 `of the kind` `the early rental-housing sale kind`, `an item of` 25 `of the kind` `the early construction sale kind`, `an item of` 75 `of the kind` `the securities kind`, `an item of` 60 `of the kind` `other income`) `, reading the 5% test as` `declined where the 5% test changes the answer` BECAUSE "section 64A2 does not say whether the whole of the other income, or only the part above 5%, is exceptional once it exceeds 5%, and here it changes the answer"
-- Other income exactly 5% (50 of 1,000): "exceeds 5%" is not met: the other income is not exceptional on either reading: 165, so the default answers.
#ASSERT `s 64A2 — the exceptional income of the fund among` (LIST `an item of` 100 `of the kind` `the inventory kind`, `an item of` 710 `of the kind` `the yielding kind`, `an item of` 40 `of the kind` `the early rental-housing sale kind`, `an item of` 25 `of the kind` `the early construction sale kind`, `an item of` 75 `of the kind` `the securities kind`, `an item of` 50 `of the kind` `other income`) `, reading the 5% test as` `declined where the 5% test changes the answer` EQUALS 165
-- Other income 51 of 1,000 (5.1%): the whole 51 (216) or the part above 50, 1 (166): the readings part.
#ASSERT `s 64A2 — the exceptional income of the fund among` (LIST `an item of` 100 `of the kind` `the inventory kind`, `an item of` 709 `of the kind` `the yielding kind`, `an item of` 40 `of the kind` `the early rental-housing sale kind`, `an item of` 25 `of the kind` `the early construction sale kind`, `an item of` 75 `of the kind` `the securities kind`, `an item of` 51 `of the kind` `other income`) `, reading the 5% test as` `all the other income is exceptional once it is more than 5%` EQUALS 216
#ASSERT `s 64A2 — the exceptional income of the fund among` (LIST `an item of` 100 `of the kind` `the inventory kind`, `an item of` 709 `of the kind` `the yielding kind`, `an item of` 40 `of the kind` `the early rental-housing sale kind`, `an item of` 25 `of the kind` `the early construction sale kind`, `an item of` 75 `of the kind` `the securities kind`, `an item of` 51 `of the kind` `other income`) `, reading the 5% test as` `only the part of the other income above 5% is exceptional` EQUALS 166
-- No item at all: nothing exceptional.
#ASSERT `s 64A2 — the exceptional income of the fund among` (EMPTY) `, reading the 5% test as` `declined where the 5% test changes the answer` EQUALS 0

§§ `Land held for a short period`
GIVEN rental  IS A BOOLEAN
      para4   IS A BOOLEAN
      bought  IS A DATE
      yielding IS A MAYBE DATE
      sold    IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A sale of land by a real-estate investment fund`
`a sale:` rental `, paragraph (4) land` para4 `, bought` bought `, yielding from` yielding `, sold` sold MEANS
    `A sale of land by a real-estate investment fund` WITH
        `it is land for rental housing` IS rental
        `it is land of paragraph (4) of the definition of land for rental housing` IS para4
        `the day the fund bought it` IS bought
        `the day it became yielding land for rental housing` IS yielding
        `the day it was sold, or sold in an exempt sale` IS sold
-- Not rental housing: bought 15 June 2020. Sold 14 June 2024 (less than four years): short. Sold 15 June 2024 (four years): not short.
#ASSERT `s 64A2 — the land sold was held for a short period` (`a sale:` FALSE `, paragraph (4) land` FALSE `, bought` (YMD 2020 6 15) `, yielding from` NOTHING `, sold` (YMD 2024 6 14))
#ASSERT NOT `s 64A2 — the land sold was held for a short period` (`a sale:` FALSE `, paragraph (4) land` FALSE `, bought` (YMD 2020 6 15) `, yielding from` NOTHING `, sold` (YMD 2024 6 15))
-- Rental housing, yielding from 1 January 2021: sold 31 December 2024 (before four years): short. Sold 1 January 2025: not short.
#ASSERT `s 64A2 — the land sold was held for a short period` (`a sale:` TRUE `, paragraph (4) land` FALSE `, bought` (YMD 2019 1 1) `, yielding from` (JUST (YMD 2021 1 1)) `, sold` (YMD 2024 12 31))
#ASSERT NOT `s 64A2 — the land sold was held for a short period` (`a sale:` TRUE `, paragraph (4) land` FALSE `, bought` (YMD 2019 1 1) `, yielding from` (JUST (YMD 2021 1 1)) `, sold` (YMD 2025 1 1))
-- Rental-housing land of paragraph (4): excluded.  Rental housing not yet yielding: not short under (2).
#ASSERT NOT `s 64A2 — the land sold was held for a short period` (`a sale:` TRUE `, paragraph (4) land` TRUE `, bought` (YMD 2019 1 1) `, yielding from` (JUST (YMD 2021 1 1)) `, sold` (YMD 2022 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT `s 64A2 — the land sold was held for a short period` (`a sale:` TRUE `, paragraph (4) land` FALSE `, bought` (YMD 2019 1 1) `, yielding from` NOTHING `, sold` (YMD 2022 1 1))
